      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-114451",
      ":question/problem": "During a company lunch, $20%$ of people choose a meal with chicken, $30%$ of people choose pork, $10%$ of people choose fish, and $40%$ choose a meal without meat. A sample of ten people is randomly selected. Find the probability that $4$ of them choose chicken, $2$ choose pork, $2$ choose fish, and $2$ choose a meal without meat. Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
