      ":question/problem": "In a store, the probability that a customer buys zero, one, two, or three or more products is $0.5$, $0.3$, $0.1$, and $0.1$, respectively. If $6$ customers enter the store, find the probability that $3$ won't buy anything, $2$ will buy one product, and $1$ will buy two products.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
